            <div xml:id="d361">

                <pb facs="0531" n="217" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg217"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/102</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé d’Affaires in Russia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">St. Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-20T14:00:00+02:30">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 20, 1914, 2 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 4:30 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Department’s August 19, 4 p.m. Russian Government still waiting for decision of
                    British Government, as it will take similar action. However, Foreign Office does
                    not expect British Government will decide to observe Declaration of London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
